  "body": "### Summary\nAs a reader of long topics, I want the legacy \"Page numéro\" sheet, with first and last page buttons and -10 / -1 / +1 / +10, so that I move a few pages without typing a five-digit number.\n\nMilestone: **M4** (validated legacy parity, ROADMAP). Source: operator UI comparison of 2026-11-11, side-by-side simulator captures 10 (pseudos redacted, attached below when available).\n\n### Observed (2026-11-11)\n- Legacy: sheet \"Page numéro\" (close, \"Valider\"), \"Choisir une page entre 1 et 1126\", first | number field (current page) | last, then -10 | -1 | +1 | +10.\n- SwiftHFR: a system alert \"Aller à la page / Entre 1 et 1126\" with an empty field, Annuler / Aller.\n\n### Legacy source @ `87fe0d1c`\n`TopicPagePickerSheet` and `TopicPagePickerQuickButton`, `HFRswift/Swift/Common.swift:3063-3190`; menu entry `:3590`.\n\n### Scope\nPort the sheet as is (parity), opened from \"Page …\" in the reader's \"⋯\" (and from the title if N4 keeps the subtitle). Field prefilled with the current page, clamped to 1…last.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] ±1 / ±10 clamp at the bounds; first / last fill the field; Valider opens the page.\n- [ ] The alert is gone.\n\nRelation with LOT-110 (#201, FEAT-002, M5): see the comment there. This issue is the parity part; LOT-110 can build on it later.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
